Two parts of the operations request are not in this implementation:

- **Log file:** a `wasm32-unknown-unknown` component with no WASI adapter has no filesystem, and none of the provided interfaces can write a file.
- **Metadata fetch:** this node is granted only `response-channel`. Importing `http-client` would give it authority its contract doesn't include, and would also send user text to an external service.

If either is needed, the graph should grant that capability to the node explicitly. The node's output is unaffected.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        response_channel::send(&reply.text)
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

